## Low-spec / weak-PC strain: LXQt (Lubuntu's desktop) instead of GNOME --
## lighter on RAM/CPU than even ubuntu-desktop-minimal. Deliberately skips
## gnome-shell-extensions/gnome-tweaks (LXQt isn't GNOME, those packages
## would be dead weight) and skips gamemode/mangohud/winetricks by default
## to keep the base image lean -- a low-spec machine running Gaming mode at
## all is the exception, not the default; modes/gaming/setup/*.sh installs
## those on demand instead of bloating every low-spec install up front.
lubuntu-desktop
## REQUIRED for the live session to autologin. lubuntu-desktop hard-depends on
## SDDM, so casper takes its SDDM branch -- but casper's Lubuntu live probe looks
## for /usr/share/xsessions/lubuntu-live-environment.desktop, which ONLY
## lubuntu-installer-prompt provides, and that is neither a Depends nor a
## Recommends of lubuntu-desktop. Without it casper finds no session to autologin
## and SDDM drops the live user at a greeter -- with no password to type, since
## casper's live user has none. The GNOME strains are unaffected (gdm branch).
lubuntu-installer-prompt
flatpak
